OL,3,GNEWSA'Massive change' as iconic sloping
OL,4,Apitch levelled
OL,5,
OL,6,FAbout 12,000 tonnes of soil has been
OL,7,Fremoved to level out a non-league
OL,8,Ffootball pitch, that previously had a
OL,9,Fnoticeable slope.
OL,11,FThe pitch at The Elms Recreation
OL,12,FGround, home to Highworth Town Football
OL,13,FClub near Swindon, has been both
OL,14,Flowered and levelled to enable the club
OL,15,Fto play on a flat surface for the first
OL,16,Ftime.
OL,18,FCommittee member Fraser Haines said it
OL,19,Fwas "a massive change" but that he
OL,20,Fstill had fond memories of the old
OL,21,Fpitch even if he knew it needed to be
OL,22,Ffixed.
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
